# Spirit Warrior

**Alignments.** Any, but most are principled or scrupulous.

The newest of the Native American O.C.C.s, appearing only since the Return of
the Ancients about 200 years ago: the Great Spirits'' monster hunter and the
ultimate defender of the Pure Ones. Where a Totem Warrior trades part of his
spirit with one Greater Spirit, the Spirit Warrior trades aspects of his with
several, and his great strength is reserved for power armor, robots, vehicles
and supernatural foes. Often a war chief, often a loner respected and feared by
his own people, and an occasional companion of the Cyber-Knights.

## Fetishes

Spirit Warriors start with one minor fetish of choice, one major fetish of
choice and a legendary Spirit Weapon Fetish - typically a spirit bow, but any
weapon may be chosen. A further minor fetish is typically awarded at levels 5
and 10, a second major one at level 5, and another for great heroism no sooner
than level 8.

## Lore

About one Spirit Warrior in eight is a woman (printed 37). They gather in
numbers in the northeast, where the spirits keep them fighting whatever emerges
from the Calgary Rift, and they are the warriors the tribes send on quests and
missions of great importance - often guided there by visions and dreams.

## Equipment the catalog cannot hold yet

A war club and a tomahawk or spear, soft moccasins, 50 feet of rope, a week of
dried meat and fruit, and war and camouflage paint. A rifle and a revolver may
suit some Traditionalists, never a Pure One.
